From 7b03948695460f318a71d683f8290b75b07a7864 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: sadatdaniel <sadatdaniel@yahoo.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 16:14:19 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] decon: let userspace force the fingerprint HBM mask layer

The A50's fingerprint sensor is an optical under-display EGISTEC ET713. It can
only image a finger while the panel lights the sensor area (high brightness
mode). On this panel that is Samsung's "mask layer":

  panels/ea8076_a50_lcd_ctrl.c
      if (decon && decon->current_mask_layer)
              lcd->brightness = lcd->mask_brightness;

and decon only sets current_mask_layer when the compositor submits a window
whose state is DECON_WIN_STATE_FINGERPRINT:

  decon_core.c decon_get_mask_layer()
      if (config && (config->state == DECON_WIN_STATE_FINGERPRINT))
              mask = true;

Android's SurfaceFlinger/HWC flags the fingerprint overlay that way. Ubuntu
Touch composites with Lomiri/Mir, which knows nothing about that state, so
current_mask_layer never becomes true, actual_mask_brightness stays 0 however
mask_brightness is written, the finger is never lit, and the sensor reports no
finger forever (bauth_FPBAuthService "nd cnt : 0").

Add a module parameter that ORs into the same decision. Everything downstream
is unchanged: the transition still runs through decon_set_mask_layer() on the
regs path, keeping its TE/vsync wait, its call_panel_ops(mask_brightness) and
its wait_mask_layer_trigger handshake. Only the trigger is new.

Defaults to false, so a kernel carrying this patch with the parameter untouched
behaves exactly as before. That makes it safe to boot-test on its own first and
only then enable the flag - one variable at a time.

  /sys/module/decon/parameters/force_mask_layer

decon_core.c already exposes module parameters this way (decon_log_level and
friends), so both the mechanism and the sysfs path are the established ones for
this file.

---
 drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu20/decon_core.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu20/decon_core.c b/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu20/decon_core.c
index ba6cb4ce3..965207d08 100644
--- a/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu20/decon_core.c
+++ b/drivers/video/fbdev/exynos/dpu20/decon_core.c
@@ -70,6 +70,16 @@ int win_update_log_level = 0;
 module_param(win_update_log_level, int, 0644);
 int dpu_mres_log_level = 0;
 module_param(dpu_mres_log_level, int, 0644);
+
+#if defined(CONFIG_SUPPORT_MASK_LAYER)
+/*
+ * Force the fingerprint HBM mask layer on, for compositors that never set
+ * DECON_WIN_STATE_FINGERPRINT (Ubuntu Touch / Lomiri-Mir). Without it the
+ * optical under-display sensor is never lit and never sees a finger.
+ */
+bool decon_force_mask_layer = false;
+module_param_named(force_mask_layer, decon_force_mask_layer, bool, 0644);
+#endif
 int decon_systrace_enable;
 
 struct decon_device *decon_drvdata[MAX_DECON_CNT];
@@ -2596,6 +2606,9 @@ static bool decon_get_mask_layer(struct decon_device *decon,
 		}
 	}
 
+	if (decon_force_mask_layer)
+		mask = true;
+
 	/* normal -> mask set wait_mask_layer_trigger */
 	/* mask -> normal set wait_mask_layer_trigger */
 	if (mask != decon->current_mask_layer) {
-- 
